; Tilo installer live-medium SELinux policy module (CIL).
; ===========================================================================
; Loaded ONLY on the installer live medium, at boot, by
; tilo-installer-setup.service (which is gated on the `tilo.install` kernel
; cmdline). The INSTALLED system never loads this module.
;
; WHY THIS EXISTS
; ---------------
; The tilo-installer UI runs under `cage` in the greetd session, whose SELinux
; domain is `xdm_t`. xdm_t is a login/desktop domain and is correctly denied
; the privileged container/install operations a whole-disk install needs.
;
; The privileged backend (tilo-install) sidesteps this by re-launching its real
; work as a TRANSIENT systemd unit (`systemd-run`), so the dangerous operations
; (bootc image copy-to-storage, `podman run --privileged ... bootc install
; to-disk`, partition/mount of the freshly written disk) execute in a
; system-service domain (init_t) — which the base targeted policy already
; permits — and stay FULLY ENFORCED. See os/usr/libexec/tilo-install.
;
; The ONLY remaining gap is that xdm_t must be allowed to ASK systemd to start
; that transient unit. This module grants exactly that, scoped to the ephemeral
; installer medium. It replaces the live medium's former global `enforcing=0`
; (os/installer-disk.toml): the whole system — including every privileged
; install operation and greeter session both remain enforcing.
;
; The enforcing VM reported a USER_AVC on StartTransientUnit with xdm_t as
; source, init_t as target, and system:start as the denied permission. Permit
; just that operation for the live installer session. The backend itself runs
; as an init_t transient service and remains enforcing.
(allow xdm_t init_t (system (start)))

; Only the live installer handoff uses this root-owned /run subtree. A
; dedicated type avoids granting the greeter access to every generic
; var_run_t file on the machine. The setup service loads this module before
; creating the directory and restorecon labels it. A transient system unit
; creates and labels each run's secret files before the greeter writes them.
(type tilo_installer_bridge_t)
(roletype object_r tilo_installer_bridge_t)
(typeattributeset file_type (tilo_installer_bridge_t))
(typeattributeset non_auth_file_type (tilo_installer_bridge_t))
(filecon "/run/tilo-installer/bridge(/.*)?" any
  (system_u object_r tilo_installer_bridge_t ((s0) (s0))))

; The greeter-side privileged wrapper traverses the private directory,
; writes the startup secret to stdin, and tails the output. It cannot create,
; delete, or relabel the bridge files. DAC keeps the directory root-only
; (0700) and its two files 0600.
(allow xdm_t tilo_installer_bridge_t (dir (getattr search read watch)))
(allow xdm_t tilo_installer_bridge_t (file (getattr open read write watch)))

; The system service creates and cleans up its own per-run subtree. PID 1
; reads stdin while setting up the installer unit and appends its output.
(allow init_t tilo_installer_bridge_t
  (dir (getattr search read write add_name remove_name create setattr rmdir)))
(allow init_t tilo_installer_bridge_t
  (file (getattr open read write append create setattr unlink)))

; Other D-Bus permissions, if live AVCs require them:
; ----------------------------------------------------------------
; Add only permissions observed in an enforcing VM run.
;
; (allow xdm_t system_dbusd_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow system_dbusd_t xdm_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow xdm_t init_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow init_t xdm_t (dbus (send_msg)))
